---
title: Crispy Roast Potatoes
description: Crisp roast potatoes, parboiled with baking soda and tossed in rosemary-garlic oil.
course: side
source:
  name: Serious Eats
  author: J. Kenji López-Alt
  url: https://www.seriouseats.com/the-best-roast-potatoes-ever-recipe
servings: 6-8
prep time: 30m
cook time: 1h15m
---

Adjust an oven rack to the center position and preheat the oven to 450°F (230°C), or 400°F (200°C) if using convection.

Heat 2 quarts (2 L) of water in a large #pot{} over high heat until boiling. Add the @kosher salt{2%tbsp}(about 1 oz or 25 g, plus more to season), @baking soda{1/2%tsp}(4 g), and @potatoes{4%lb}(about 2 kg, russet or Yukon gold, peeled and cut into quarters, sixths, or eighths, depending on size) and stir. Return to a boil, reduce to a simmer, and cook until a knife meets little resistance when inserted into a potato chunk, about ~simmer{10%minutes} after returning to a boil.

Meanwhile, combine the @extra-virgin olive oil{5%tbsp}(75 ml, or duck fat, goose fat, or beef fat) with the @rosemary leaves{1%handful}(small, picked, finely chopped), @garlic cloves{3}(medium, minced), and a few grinds of @black pepper{}(freshly ground) in a #small saucepan{} and heat over medium heat. Cook, stirring and shaking the pan constantly, until the garlic just begins to turn golden, about ~cook{3%minutes}.

Immediately strain the oil through a #fine-mesh strainer{} set in a #large bowl{}. Set the garlic and rosemary mixture aside and reserve separately.

When the potatoes are cooked, drain carefully and let them rest in the pot for about ~rest{30%seconds} to allow excess moisture to evaporate. Transfer to the bowl with the infused oil, season to taste with a little more salt and pepper, and toss to coat, shaking the bowl roughly, until a thick layer of mashed potato–like paste has built up on the potato chunks.

Transfer the potatoes to a large rimmed #baking sheet{} and separate them, spreading them out evenly. Transfer to the oven and roast, without moving, for ~roast{20%minutes}.

Using a thin, flexible metal #spatula{} to release any stuck potatoes, shake the pan and turn the potatoes. Continue roasting until the potatoes are deep brown and crisp all over, turning and shaking them a few times during cooking, ~roast{30-40%minutes} longer.

Transfer the potatoes to a #&large bowl{} and add the garlic and rosemary mixture and the @fresh parsley leaves{1%handful}(small, minced). Toss to coat and season with more salt and pepper to taste. Serve immediately.
